WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:05.120
- Good morning Believe Nation,
today's message is Be Driven.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.099
Over to you, Shakira.
(roosting crowing)

00:00:09.099 --> 00:00:11.647
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:11.647 --> 00:00:14.542
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:14.542 --> 00:00:18.496
♫ I wake up every monrin'

00:00:18.496 --> 00:00:19.878
- You know I grew up in Columbia.

00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:23.222
And Columbia is a developing country

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:26.851
where a lot of people don't
have access to the most

00:00:26.851 --> 00:00:31.399
basic needs and where education
is considered a luxury.

00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:33.983
Unfortunately because we
all know that education is

00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:38.066
a birthright and I just
grew up frustrated seeing

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.740
how many people weren't able
to realize their own dreams.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.577
When I was eight years old,
my dad over went an economic

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.880
crisis, a financial crisis,
he lost his business.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.592
And we struggled
economically for many years.

00:00:58.592 --> 00:01:01.842
We lost our car, we lost our furniture.

00:01:04.057 --> 00:01:06.807
And I remember vividly the
day I walked in my house

00:01:06.807 --> 00:01:08.519
and all the furniture was
gone because my dad had

00:01:08.519 --> 00:01:12.686
to pay his debts and it was
quite well, shocking for me.

00:01:15.191 --> 00:01:17.653
I was eight, seven, eight years old.

00:01:17.653 --> 00:01:20.072
And when I saw this I was so frustrated

00:01:20.072 --> 00:01:22.408
and so upset with my
parents because I couldn't

00:01:22.408 --> 00:01:25.620
understand how they did
so poorly in business.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.330
I'm like, why, why, I couldn't get it.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:32.790
And my dad and my mom took me to the park

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.213
where they showed me other
kids my age sniffing glue.

00:01:36.213 --> 00:01:40.719
They were orphans, they had
no one to watch after them

00:01:40.719 --> 00:01:44.095
and they were barefoot and
they were abandoned to their

00:01:44.095 --> 00:01:48.095
own luck and it probably
left such an impression

00:01:49.557 --> 00:01:54.399
in my impressionable mind
at that age that I remember

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:57.732
that day and I remember that
I made myself a promise.

00:01:57.732 --> 00:02:01.649
I said to myself, Shakira,
you have to succeed.

00:02:02.698 --> 00:02:06.781
Because you have to ride
in a car again, one day.

00:02:08.738 --> 00:02:11.955
You have to get your own car someday.

00:02:11.955 --> 00:02:16.505
And I wanted to vindicate
my parents socially

00:02:16.505 --> 00:02:19.425
and economically and I
also wanted to someday

00:02:19.425 --> 00:02:22.727
do something for those kids
who I saw that day in the park.

00:02:22.727 --> 00:02:26.235
So as soon as I had my
first big success with

00:02:26.235 --> 00:02:30.320
Pies Descalzos which was my third album,

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.036
I decided to establish my own foundation

00:02:32.036 --> 00:02:35.044
and do my own contribution to the change

00:02:35.044 --> 00:02:37.928
even if it was going to be a small one.

00:02:37.928 --> 00:02:41.686
But I wanted to be active and
that's how it all started.

00:02:41.686 --> 00:02:45.152
Going through my own financial struggle

00:02:45.152 --> 00:02:47.779
and the struggle of my
family and understanding

00:02:47.779 --> 00:02:51.779
that the one thing that
I never lacked was care,

00:02:52.747 --> 00:02:55.623
protection and an education
and that's probably

00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:58.083
what made me thrive in life.

00:02:58.083 --> 00:03:00.085
- Having a why is so
important to accomplishing

00:03:00.085 --> 00:03:03.213
any big thing, especially
having success in business.

00:03:03.213 --> 00:03:05.634
You have to know why you're
doing something if you're

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.138
going to continue, too many
people start a business just

00:03:08.138 --> 00:03:09.598
because they're trying to make money.

00:03:09.598 --> 00:03:12.142
You may be in debt, you
may need to pay your bills.

00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:14.226
So I'm going to start a company to do it.

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:16.350
It's not a strong enough
why, what ends up happening

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.650
to the people that are
just motivated by money,

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.482
what they do is they
start a company, sometimes

00:03:20.482 --> 00:03:22.611
they'll have success, they'll
make a little bit of money,

00:03:22.611 --> 00:03:25.833
just enough to pay their
bills and then they ease off.

00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:29.255
They ease off the throttle,
they stop pushing hard.

00:03:29.255 --> 00:03:31.425
Because they've paid off
their bills until the bills

00:03:31.425 --> 00:03:33.349
come again and then they work harder.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:35.183
And these people who
are motivated by money

00:03:35.183 --> 00:03:37.473
are just living paycheck
to paycheck to paycheck

00:03:37.473 --> 00:03:40.438
to paycheck and they never
get the money they're after.

00:03:40.438 --> 00:03:43.775
You have to understand what
it is that you stand for

00:03:43.775 --> 00:03:46.490
and what big thing you're
trying to accomplish.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.706
If you can't make that
connection to the work you're

00:03:48.706 --> 00:03:51.256
doing every day, guess what,
you're going to stop working.

00:03:51.256 --> 00:03:53.756
You're not going to put
everything you've got into it.

00:03:53.756 --> 00:03:56.425
'Cause there's no strong why behind it.

00:03:56.425 --> 00:03:58.637
When I look at my first
business, I struggled a lot.

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:02.523
Right, I was making $300 a
month, barely able to survive

00:04:02.523 --> 00:04:04.109
and I told my partner that I quit.

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:06.529
You guys have heard the story
a couple times probably.

00:04:06.529 --> 00:04:09.693
I told my partner that I quit.

00:04:09.693 --> 00:04:11.117
And I woke up the next
day and I'm like, I'm not

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:14.196
going to be a quitter, I
need to see this through.

00:04:14.196 --> 00:04:17.614
I don't want to live the
rest of my life in regret.

00:04:17.614 --> 00:04:22.538
I had a situation the year
before where there was a moment

00:04:22.538 --> 00:04:24.962
that I regretted not taking
actino when I should've.

00:04:24.962 --> 00:04:27.212
I was afraid, I didn't have the courage.

00:04:27.212 --> 00:04:29.430
So I didn't take action and
I took a picture of that

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:32.347
moment and I hung it on my
wall as a reminder to myself

00:04:32.347 --> 00:04:34.765
that the next time I want
to do something and I'm too

00:04:34.765 --> 00:04:38.187
afraid to do it, I have to
go and take that chance.

00:04:38.187 --> 00:04:40.853
Because the regret will eat you up.

00:04:40.853 --> 00:04:42.731
'Cause I can deal with it not working out.

00:04:42.731 --> 00:04:44.529
I can deal with the failure
but I can't deal with

00:04:44.529 --> 00:04:48.696
not knowing, the immediate
pain of rejection or failure

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.370
sucks but it's nothing
compared to the lifetime of

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:57.580
regret you'll have always
looking back on that moment

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.586
and knowing you should've done something.

00:04:59.586 --> 00:05:03.502
So I went back to my company,
after that first experience,

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:07.709
I went back to my business
because I didn't want to leave

00:05:07.709 --> 00:05:11.215
feeling like I could do a little bit more.

00:05:11.215 --> 00:05:13.387
I've got a little bit more in
me, I didn't want to live with

00:05:13.387 --> 00:05:17.265
regret, what's your why,
if you are not getting up

00:05:17.265 --> 00:05:20.727
daily and pounding on
your business, you don't

00:05:20.727 --> 00:05:24.568
have a strong enough why so tap into it.

00:05:24.568 --> 00:05:27.276
What is it, what do you
stand for, what are you

00:05:27.276 --> 00:05:29.112
trying to build, why is it
so important that's it's

00:05:29.112 --> 00:05:31.278
a must for you to go out
and accomplish today?

00:05:31.278 --> 00:05:33.700
And I would put that
into my daily routine.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.866
You wake up, at least for
me, I need to reset everyday.

00:05:37.866 --> 00:05:41.862
You wake up and start
thinking about why am I doing

00:05:41.862 --> 00:05:44.689
what I'm doing, why am I doing
what I'm about to do today?

00:05:44.689 --> 00:05:47.197
Why is it so important to me?

00:05:47.197 --> 00:05:51.621
And if you can't come up
with an amazing reason,

00:05:51.621 --> 00:05:54.462
you're going to mail in today,
you're just not going to work hard.

00:05:54.462 --> 00:05:57.002
You're going to do enough to
get by and you're going to be

00:05:57.002 --> 00:05:59.922
one of those people who
lives paycheck to paycheck

00:05:59.922 --> 00:06:03.474
to paycheck, you want to
increase your standard of living.

00:06:03.474 --> 00:06:05.730
You want to increase the impact
that you're having on the

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.312
world, you want to increase
your level of fulfillment

00:06:07.312 --> 00:06:10.729
and happiness, have a more important why.

00:06:11.695 --> 00:06:15.741
So the question today is what is you why.

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:17.077
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:06:17.077 --> 00:06:18.369
super curious to find out.

00:06:18.369 --> 00:06:20.615
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Figrie Rahman.

00:06:20.615 --> 00:06:21.913
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my

00:06:21.913 --> 00:06:24.921
book, Your One Word, it
really, really, really

00:06:24.921 --> 00:06:27.795
means a lot to me and I hope
you're enjoying the read.

00:06:27.795 --> 00:06:29.175
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:29.175 --> 00:06:31.175
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe

00:06:31.175 --> 00:06:34.345
in yourself and whatever your one word is.

00:06:34.345 --> 00:06:37.055
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:37.055 --> 00:06:39.981
for another shot of Ent Spresso.

